<http://data.silknow.org/object/73d46a08-0c7b-30e2-ac8a-3331d30f3934/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The main figure group, including the man, woman, and infant in her arms, was taken from an engraving by Albrecht Dürer.  A procession of four figures, a man, a woman with infant, a child, standing under an oak and a dog moves right to left across a dark blue field strewn with flowering plants. The man dressed in doublet, cloak, turban, and boots, and holding a bow and two arrows, leads the procession. The woman wearing a mantle knotted over her right shoulder, a turban-like headdress, and sandals walks next to him. She carries a nude infant in her arms. The child, dressed in a tunic, hurries after the woman and pulls at her mantle. In the foreground a short haired dog walks in the same direction."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/73d46a08-0c7b-30e2-ac8a-3331d30f3934> .

